Contributing packages: [Verified elasticity and thermal models](../features/Continuum.lingua)

## Scheduling interpretation

The linked packages own implementation and its task order. This Record preserves the full source requirements, interface details, examples, research, milestones, fixtures, failure cases and completion evidence. Its `#requires` edges mean all contributors are needed to close this whole contract, not that every consumer waits for this join. Former references to earlier/later stages, delivery cycles or deferred tails describe the appropriate capability subset and composed proofs; they do not restore the removed global sequence. Incomplete unrelated siblings are not regression failures. All already verified affected capabilities must continue working.

For a mixed milestone, each contributor records its verified subset, then this join runs the actual composed workflow when all contributors exist. Do not mark the full milestone done from a local helper or silently drop geographic/hosted/numerical portions. Published exports remain usable without reopening their implementation solely to await this join; fixes to real interface defects remain mandatory.


Finish able to configure and inspect a bounded verified elastic study, steady heat conduction and transient heating/cooling from captured inputs. The user sees supported conditions, quantitative error and energy/balance evidence; motion cooling of Sands remains a separate existing behavior.

## Required workflow milestones

- [ ] **19.M01.** Set supported material regions, loads/supports and boundary maps on an accepted part; solve the named elastic patch/bar/cantilever cases and inspect source-mapped deformation/fields with honest convergence and applicability.

- [ ] **19.M02.** Set conductivity, capacity/density, initial temperature, source power and supported thermal boundaries; compare steady slab flux and transient heating with the independent reference and energy/time-refinement checks.

- [ ] **19.M03.** Cancel, exhaust a quota, change source/conditions or supply singular/unsupported inputs. Preserve accepted sources, expose failed/incomplete/stale states and never display them as passed current results.

- [ ] **19.M04.** Reopen captured inputs/results offline and share only permitted outputs with a weak visitor. Solver/run costs remain independently admitted and do not starve ordinary workspace navigation/editing.

- [ ] **19.M05.** For a declared nearly uniform-temperature case, compare a lumped thermal model with the supported spatial model, choose either through the shared inspector and transfer supported thermal state at a safe boundary. Expose the lumped approximation's validity/error and reject it when the selected gradients or requested outputs require spatial resolution.

